{
  "about": "The rule of thumb for reading a book back, as numbers, shared by the two programs that hold it: packages/application/src/replay-cost.ts (the service, which says it in GET /api/capacity and the warm-up) and apps/terminal/internal/service/capacity.go (rastrata doctor, which says it when the service does not, and scales the replay a verified backup timed). Both are held to these numbers, so a constant cannot be changed in one and forgotten in the other. A snapshot is {bytes, sequence}: its size and the ledger entry it was saved at. Seconds are the expected results to six places. See docs/reference/program/scale/scaleestimates.md for where each constant came from.",
